      "discrepancies": [
        {
          "id": "terah-abram-age-puzzle",
          "traditions_involved": [
            "mt",
            "lxx",
            "sp"
          ],
          "type": "uncertain",
          "confidence": "high",
          "description": "Genesis 11:26 says Terah was 70 when he fathered Abram, Nahor, and Haran (listed together, birth order not stated). But Terah died at 205 (11:32, MT/LXX), and Acts 7:4 says Abram left Haran only AFTER his father's death, at age 75 (Genesis 12:4) -- which requires Terah to have been 130, not 70, specifically when ABRAM was born. Standard resolution: Abram is listed first by covenant significance, not birth order, and was actually the youngest of the three, born when Terah was 130.",
          "theological_significance": "SP's total for Terah is 145, not 205 -- and 70 (age when Terah began fathering) + 75 (Abram's age at departure, Gen 12:4) = 145 exactly. If SP's total is correct, Terah's death coincides exactly with Abram's departure without needing the '130 at Abram's specific birth' reinterpretation at all -- SP resolves the puzzle a completely different way than the standard MT-based harmonization does. This is the single most consequential textual variant found in this whole survey for reconstructing Abram's actual birth-year and the true length of the post-Flood genealogy."
        }
      ],
